  "faithful": "This remainder therefore is nothing but a mixture of alum and charnels. Now, at the acid of the fils, which is the vitrific, bath a greater affinity with the phologlinium than with any other fulbiance, it will quit its balls to unite with the phologlin of the coal, and be converted by that some into a fulphur. And that is the very cold of which we have certain proofs in the operation for preparing this phorhons; the whom, after the volatile principle of the only matter we drawn off, the fire is increased, in order to combine closely together the fixed parts that remain in the matras, that is, the alum and the shared matter, we perceive at the mouth of the matras a final fillon fulphourtsome, and a pungent finish of burning fulphar. Noy, when the operation is finih",
